## Worksheet

F1: Game class instance `game` holds all state; mulberry32(seed) rng used for map/colonists/events/storm, no Math.random anywhere; endTurn() runs event roll -> runProduction() -> runConsumption() -> updateColonistStates() -> storm check -> trade caravan -> loss check -> win check, fixed order every call. Score 2.

F2: generateMap() loops 8x8, terrain chosen by weighted this.rng() roll against terrainWeights; buildBuilding() rejects `tile.terrain !== building.terrain`; getAdjacencyBonuses() sets building.adjBonus, read back in runProduction() as `output += output*adjBonus/100` - a real production change. Score 2.

F3: partsFab.needs = ['metal','power'] to produce parts - metal (forge/smelter output) feeds a second building, a genuine two-step chain. But runProduction() consumes each needed resource by a hardcoded flat `resources[res]--` (1 unit) regardless of output size - not scaled. storageCaps enforced with overflow logged. Chain is real but consumption math is shallow/hardcoded. Score 1.

F4: colonist records carry id/name/job/skill/fatigue/morale/assigned. skill is read in runProduction() (`skillSum += c.skill`, feeds output). fatigue is written in updateColonistStates() and read only in display (renderPeople) and range tests (runTests) - never read by any production/output code. Score 1.

F5: runConsumption() computes food/water deficits, applies `c.morale -= 5` per shortage - a real, non-instant state change. But grep for morale usage shows it is never read inside runProduction() or any output formula - shortage lowers morale but morale never lowers output. Score 1.

F6: RESEARCH_NODES has 12 nodes with prereq chains and costs, and `research[node.id].done` exists as a field. Grepping the whole file, the only place `done` is ever compared is a read (prereq check at line 1083, and score/end-screen tallies) - nothing ever sets `research[x].done = true`. The only Research-tab control is `onclick="alert('TODO: Research mechanics')"`. Purchase mechanic does not exist in any form. Score 0.

F7: 15 events defined, each with a `weight` field, but grepping `.weight` across the file shows zero reads of it outside the EVENTS array literal itself - fireEvent() does `EVENTS[Math.floor(this.rng()*EVENTS.length)]`, a uniform pick. `this.eventCooldown = {}` is assigned once at construction and never read or written again. Of the 6 choice-events, only 'desertion' (popLoss vs moraleLoss) has both branches doing distinct real mutations; outbreak/equipment/mutation/outsiders/accident each route at least one choice to the generic `// TODO: Implement remaining outcomes` no-op case in resolveEvent()'s switch default. Score 1.

F8: renderTrade()'s caravanGoods is a hardcoded literal array (fixed price/stock numbers) - never reads this.resources or any supply variable, stock is never decremented anywhere. The only Buy control is `onclick="alert('TODO: Buy/sell mechanics')"` - no buy or sell function exists in the file at all. Score 0.

F9: triggerStorm() scales `severity = min(5, floor(turn/15)+1)`, computes damage from severity, reduces it by `shieldCount*5` for Storm Shield buildings, and runProduction() applies `output * (health/maxHealth)` so damaged buildings genuinely produce less. But the only Repair control is `onclick="alert('TODO: Repair/dismantle mechanics')"` - no repair function exists anywhere, so building health only ever decreases, never recovers, and "repair costs resources" is entirely absent. Score 1.

F10: getSaveState()/loadFromState() exist and are exercised only by runTests()'s internal Test 11 round-trip check. There is no `<textarea>`, no Save/Load button, and no pasted-text import path anywhere in the DOM or JS - a code comment even says "Save/load via JSON textarea" but no such textarea exists in the HTML. The player-facing feature the rubric describes does not exist. Score 0.

F11: endTurn() checks `this.colonists.length === 0` (loss, reachable via popLoss event branches) and `this.turn >= 60 && this.colonists.length >= 12` (win, reachable via popGain/birth/outsiders-accept). showEndScreen() computes score from colonists.length, completed-research count, three summed resources, and turn, then renders a modal end screen with those stats. All parts present and reachable. Score 2.

F12: switchTab() toggles `.active` on buttons/panels; addLog() stores `{turn, text, type}` and renderLog() prefixes each line `T{turn}:`; a keydown listener wires Space (end turn) and keys 1-5 (tab switching); a `@media (max-width: 768px)` block resizes sidebar/tiles/grids. Grepping "tooltip" finds only the CSS class definition - no JS anywhere creates, positions, or fills a tooltip element to explain a number. Score 1.

F13: runTests() has 15 assertions on real invariants (resource non-negativity, storage caps, research-prereq consistency, colonist morale/fatigue/skill ranges, map dimensions, save/load round-trip equality, adjacency bonus presence, event outcome shape, RNG reproducibility) - not trivial checks. runBenchmark() constructs a fresh Game and calls `bench.endTurn()` 200 times, then prints `hashState(bench.getSaveState())`. However endTurn() unconditionally calls `this.render()` on its normal path, and render() calls `document.getElementById(...)` repeatedly against the live page DOM - the "benchmark" is not actually decoupled from the UI, it drives the real DOM 200 times as a side effect. Score 1.

G1: runProduction() contains the literal comment `// TODO: Apply research bonuses from unlocked techs` immediately after applying adjacency bonus, and the function never reads `this.research` anywhere. Combined with F6 (research can never even be marked done), no research effect ever reaches a production formula. Score 0.

G2: runConsumption() writes `c.morale -= 5` on food/water deficit - a real, traceable state mutation, not just a log line. But runProduction()'s output formula reads only `building.workers`, colonist `.skill`, `adjBonus`, and `health/maxHealth` - `c.morale` appears nowhere in it, so the chain snaps at the final link (morale never reduces labor output). Score 1.

G3: triggerStorm() sets `building.health -= damage` for every non-shield building; runProduction() applies `output * (building.health/building.maxHealth)`, so storm -> damage -> output loss is a real, traceable pipeline through actual production code, not a hardcoded special case. But "repair costs resources; restores output" is completely absent - the only Repair control is an `alert('TODO: Repair/dismantle mechanics')` stub, so damaged buildings never recover. Score 2.

G4: renderTrade()'s caravanGoods array hardcodes price 2/3/8/5/15 per good, never reading this.resources or any variable that drifts over turns; there is also no buy/sell function to exercise a price against player stockpiles at all. Link does not exist in code. Score 0.

G5: resolveEvent()'s 'desertion' event durably diverges: popLoss splices a colonist out of `this.colonists`, moraleLoss lowers every colonist's morale by 20 - two real, different mutations from one event's choices. But of the other 5 choice-events, each routes at least one choice branch to the shared TODO case in the switch default, which only calls addLog() with no state mutation - so only one event fully qualifies as "2+ choices, both durably different." Score 2.

